      "updated": 1787413216887,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "STRATEGY : \n1. Should we use minHeap or\nmaxHeap ?ANS :  minHeap \n\n2. Now how we will use minheap\n-> first make a heap till kth\nelement -> means heap of size\n2\n\n3. then add other elements one\nby one , the size of heap\nshould not be extend k \n\n4. now suppose 1 came, don't\ngive entry , now 5 came ,give\nhim entry , only give entry when\narray[i] is greater than peek\nelement",
      "fontSize": 16.01295725699043,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "STRATEGY : \n1. Should we use minHeap or maxHeap ?ANS :  minHeap \n\n2. Now how we will use minheap\n-> first make a heap till kth element -> means heap of size 2\n\n3. then add other elements one by one , the size of heap should not be extend k \n\n4. now suppose 1 came, don't give entry , now 5 came ,give him entry , only give entry when array[i] is greater than peek element",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
